 "means": "for every corpus round whose bag 1 is harddrop's Gamushiro Stacking bag 1 cell for cell (as drawn or mirrored, the L stood on the O at 7 locks or held at 6), the deepest node of that page's second-bag forms and third-bag Perfect Clears the round reaches, and how often each node's sampling point was reached. A reference opener: the corpus barely plays it",
 "not_eligible_because": "every board is the vendored Triangle engine's; which bag-2 and later shape was built has no second implementation. The Perfect Clear COUNT is anchored by perfect_clear_timing, the shape is not.",
 "caveat": "bag-1 opportunities count rounds that reached the sampling point clean (inside the verified prefix, no clear, no garbage before it); bag-2 opportunities allow garbage: complete garbage rows are stripped from the bottom of the board first (garbage_rows_stripped). PC patterns have no separate sampling point and count the rounds that reached their anchor, the form family. A hold is asserted only by the lock-7 piece test. There is no harddrop opener field for this opener, so no flag. Form D is taller than 8 rows and is not compared. Only the page's second bag and its 8-line Perfect Clears are transcribed; its other continuations are not. bag2_near is measured against the board before the TST, never a match.",
